# Local development environment template.
#
# You usually do NOT need a .env file locally. `bun run dev` works with zero
# configuration: it defaults to SQLite at .tmp/dev.db and skips Docker entirely.
#
# Copy this file to .env (or export the variables in your shell) ONLY if you
# want to override the defaults below.

PORT=3001

# Comma-separated CIDRs for reverse proxies whose X-Forwarded-For header may
# be trusted. Leave empty for direct/local development.
# TRUSTED_PROXY_CIDRS=127.0.0.1/32,::1/128

# ─── Database ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Default: SQLite at .tmp/dev.db (no Docker, no Postgres process).
# Set DATABASE_URL only if you want to use Postgres or a custom SQLite path.
#
#   SQLite (file):    DATABASE_URL=sqlite:./path/to/your.db
#   SQLite (memory):  DATABASE_URL=sqlite::memory:
#   Postgres (auto):  DATABASE_URL=postgres://instatic:instatic@127.0.0.1:5433/instatic
#                     (`bun run dev` will start the Docker postgres service automatically)
#
# DATABASE_URL=sqlite:./.tmp/dev.db

# ─── Filesystem paths ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
UPLOADS_DIR=./uploads
STATIC_DIR=./dist

# ─── Multi-tenant serving (optional) ─────────────────────────────────────────
# Apex domain that merchant sites are served under as <slug>.<PUBLIC_BASE_DOMAIN>.
# A site's own custom_domain always resolves regardless of this. Unset → every
# public request serves the default site (single-tenant).
# PUBLIC_BASE_DOMAIN=shopzoon.app

# ─── Published output → object storage (optional) ────────────────────────────
# Push each publish to an S3-compatible bucket under sites/<siteId>/… (for CDN /
# edge serving). Works with AWS S3, Cloudflare R2, MinIO, RustFS, etc. All four
# of ENDPOINT/BUCKET/ACCESS_KEY_ID/SECRET_ACCESS_KEY must be set to enable it;
# unset → publishes stay on local disk only. The endpoint is the base server URL
# (path-style — no bucket in it). REGION defaults to "auto"; set us-east-1 for
# MinIO/RustFS. Objects are uploaded PRIVATE — make the bucket/prefix public-
# readable (e.g. `mc anonymous set download <alias>/<bucket>`) or front it with a
# credentialed CDN to serve them.
# PUBLISH_STORAGE_ENDPOINT=http://localhost:9000
# PUBLISH_STORAGE_BUCKET=published-sites
# PUBLISH_STORAGE_ACCESS_KEY_ID=
# PUBLISH_STORAGE_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY=
# PUBLISH_STORAGE_REGION=us-east-1

# ─── AI credential encryption ───────────────────────────────────────────────
# Local dev auto-creates .tmp/secret.key. Production deployments must set
# INSTATIC_SECRET_KEY to the output of:
#
#   bun run scripts/generate-secret-key.ts
#
# INSTATIC_SECRET_KEY=

# ─── Authentication (Logto OIDC) ─────────────────────────────────────────────
# The admin app authenticates through Logto — the builder is the OIDC client.
# Create a "Traditional Web" application in your Logto tenant and copy its
# App ID / App Secret here. Define organization roles named `owner` and
# `admin` in Logto and assign them inside each organization — the builder maps
# those organization roles onto editable sites.
#
# Auth endpoints are unconfigured-safe: the server still boots without these,
# but /admin/api/cms/auth/login returns a 500 until they are set.
#
# LOGTO_ENDPOINT=https://your-tenant.logto.app
# LOGTO_APP_ID=
# LOGTO_APP_SECRET=
#
# The redirect + post-logout URIs are derived from PUBLIC_ORIGIN as
# `<origin>/admin/api/cms/auth/callback` and `<origin>/admin`. Set PUBLIC_ORIGIN
# (below) or override the URIs explicitly. Register the callback URL in the
# Logto application's "Redirect URIs" and the post-logout URL in "Post sign-out
# redirect URIs".
#
# PUBLIC_ORIGIN=http://localhost:3001
# LOGTO_REDIRECT_URI=
# LOGTO_POST_LOGOUT_REDIRECT_URI=
# LOGTO_SCOPES is optional. If set, the builder still appends the required
# Logto organization scopes for membership + organization-role claims.
# LOGTO_SCOPES=openid profile email roles
